<div class="trustline container"><p>Designed for real education workflows</p><div class="trust-items"><span><b>✦</b> Claude-focused AI</span><span><b>◈</b> Educator-led</span><span><b>◎</b> Multilingual learning</span><span><b>▦</b> Data-informed support</span></div></div>
<section class="section section-alt" id="solutions"><div class="container"><div class="section-center reveal"><div class="eyebrow">What we're building</div><h2 class="section-title">Four solutions.<br>One connected learning experience.</h2><p class="section-copy">From an enrollment inquiry to a student's next speaking exercise, our product direction connects everyday education work with thoughtful AI assistance.</p></div><div class="feature-grid">
<article class="feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-top"><div class="feature-icon">↗</div><span class="status">Product concept</span></div><h3>Bright Workflow AI</h3><p>Help school teams manage repetitive inquiries, enrollment steps, student communications, reminders, and reports — with staff approval built into sensitive workflows.</p><div class="feature-tags"><span>Student inquiries</span><span>Onboarding</span><span>AI task workflows</span></div><div class="mock-mini"><div class="mini-ui"><div class="ui-label">Student requests <span style="float:right;color:#98a4b4;font-weight:500">Today · Demo</span></div><div class="ui-row"><div class="ui-bubble">KT</div><div class="ui-text"></div><span class="ui-state">Draft ready</span></div><div class="ui-row"><div class="ui-bubble">MS</div><div class="ui-text short"></div><span class="ui-state">Reviewed</span></div><div class="ui-row"><div class="ui-bubble">AL</div><div class="ui-text"></div><span class="ui-state">Draft ready</span></div></div></div></article>
<article class="feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-top"><div class="feature-icon">✎</div><span class="status">Product concept</span></div><h3>Bright Teaching AI</h3><p>Turn curriculum topics into teacher-editable lesson plans, graded Japanese exercises, reading passages, and formative assessments designed around learning objectives.</p><div class="feature-tags"><span>Lesson preparation</span><span>JLPT-aligned exercises</span><span>Teacher review</span></div><div class="mock-mini"><div class="mini-ui"><div class="ui-label">Lesson builder <span style="float:right;color:#98a4b4;font-weight:500">Draft · Demo</span></div><div class="lessonpill"><span>Japanese · N4</span><span>Grammar</span><span>45 minutes</span></div><div class="lessonitem">✓ Learning objective: explain ～ようになる</div><div class="lessonitem">✓ Example dialogue and guided practice</div><div class="lessonitem">✓ Five-question comprehension check</div></div></div></article>
<article class="feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-top"><div class="feature-icon">◉</div><span class="status">Product concept</span></div><h3>Bright Conversation AI</h3><p>Practice Japanese through realistic everyday, classroom, and workplace scenarios. Receive tailored suggestions on word choice, clarity, politeness, and next steps.</p><div class="feature-tags"><span>Scenario role-play</span><span>Japanese communication</span><span>Personalized feedback</span></div><div class="mock-mini"><div class="mini-ui"><div class="ui-label">Conversation practice <span style="float:right;color:#98a4b4;font-weight:500">Apartment viewing · Demo</span></div><div class="chat-row">こんにちは。今日はお部屋の見学ですね。</div><div class="chat-row reply">はい、よろしくお願いします。駅まで何分ですか。</div><div style="font-size:9px;color:#6677bf;margin-top:11px">✦ Feedback: Natural, polite question for this situation.</div></div></div></article>
<article class="feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-top"><div class="feature-icon">▥</div><span class="status">Product concept</span></div><h3>Bright Learning Analytics</h3><p>Bring assessment results and practice history together to help educators spot learning gaps, follow progress, and plan more targeted support for each learner.</p><div class="feature-tags"><span>Progress summaries</span><span>Learning gaps</span><span>Educator insights</span></div><div class="mock-mini"><div class="mini-ui"><div class="ui-label">Skill development <span style="float:right;color:#98a4b4;font-weight:500">Illustrative scores</span></div><div class="bars"><span style="height:42%"></span><span style="height:63%"></span><span style="height:56%"></span><span style="height:72%"></span><span style="height:68%"></span><span style="height:85%"></span><span style="height:94%"></span></div><div class="chart-labels"><span>Week 01</span><span>Week 07</span></div></div></div></article>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="approach"><div class="container split"><div class="reveal"><div class="eyebrow">Our philosophy</div><h2 class="section-title">AI does the busywork.<br>People lead the learning.</h2><p class="section-copy">We focus on AI workflows that are helpful in a real school, not just impressive in a demo. Each proposed experience is designed around trusted learning materials, useful feedback, and clear human decision-making.</p><div class="stack"><div class="stack-item"><div class="stack-icon">✓</div><div><h4>Grounded in approved materials</h4><p>Teaching and administrative assistance should use institution-provided policies and curriculum rather than unsupported assumptions.</p></div></div><div class="stack-item"><div class="stack-icon">◎</div><div><h4>Human review where it matters</h4><p>Teachers remain responsible for lessons, assessments, and advice; staff approve sensitive student communications.</p></div></div><div class="stack-item"><div class="stack-icon">✧</div><div><h4>Built for multilingual contexts</h4><p>Our initial focus includes Japanese learning and communication needs common among international students.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flow-card reveal"><div class="flow-top"><div class="flow-title">Proposed workflow</div><div class="flow-line"><div class="flow-node">Curriculum</div><span class="flow-arr">+</span><div class="flow-node">School policies</div><span class="flow-arr">+</span><div class="flow-node">Learner needs</div></div></div><div class="flow-down"></div><div class="ai-center"><div class="spark">✳</div><h3>Claude-powered assistance</h3><p>Task-focused agents · Structured workflows · Quality checks</p></div><div class="flow-down"></div><div class="flow-bottom"><div>◈ &nbsp; Educator review</div><div>▥ &nbsp; Learning insights</div></div><p style="font-size:10px;color:#9aa6bb;line-height:1.7;margin:20px 0 0">Architecture illustration — proposed design, not a claim of live Claude integrations.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-alt" id="use-cases"><div class="container"><div class="section-center reveal"><div class="eyebrow">Real-world focus</div><h2 class="section-title">Built around everyday<br>teaching challenges.</h2><p class="section-copy">We start with situations educational teams already recognize — and design AI assistance around the people responsible for the outcome.</p></div><div class="case-grid"><article class="case reveal"><div class="case-num">01 / INSTITUTIONS</div><h3>Student enrollment support</h3><p>A Japanese language school needs to answer repeated questions about required documents, intake timelines, and enrollment steps. AI drafts responses from approved guidance for staff to check and send.</p><div class="case-foot">Less repetitive administration →</div></article><article class="case reveal"><div class="case-num">02 / EDUCATORS</div><h3>Lesson preparation</h3><p>A teacher preparing an N4 class requests dialogue prompts, vocabulary exercises, and short quizzes for a specific grammar point, then refines the draft to match the classroom.</p><div class="case-foot">More time for actual teaching →</div></article><article class="case reveal"><div class="case-num">03 / LEARNERS</div><h3>Confidence through practice</h3><p>An international student rehearses a conversation with a landlord, workplace supervisor, or school office and receives clear guidance on natural expressions and politeness.</p><div class="case-foot">Practice beyond the classroom →</div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="about"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="reveal"><div class="eyebrow">About bright education</div><h2 class="section-title">Practical innovation.<br>Purposeful impact.</h2><p class="section-copy">Bright Education JSC. is an emerging education technology initiative exploring how modern language models and AI agents can support institutions, teachers, and learners. Our initial product direction concentrates on Japanese language education, multilingual communication, routine school processes, and measurable learning support.</p><p class="section-copy">Rather than replace teachers, we aim to give them better tools: simpler workflows, flexible content creation, guided practice, and clearer information for instructional decisions.</p></div><div class="reveal"><div style="padding:34px;background:#f8faff;border:1px solid #e8ecf5;border-radius:20px"><div class="eyebrow">Development direction</div><div class="roadmap" style="display:block;margin-top:32px"><div class="road" style="margin-bottom:25px"><small>PHASE 01</small><h3>Product research & validation</h3><p>Define institutional needs, map educational workflows, and create representative interface and AI interaction prototypes.</p></div><div class="road" style="margin-bottom:25px"><small>PHASE 02</small><h3>Focused MVP development</h3><p>Build selected teaching support, language practice, and workflow assistance features with evaluation and review checkpoints.</p></div><div class="road"><small>PHASE 03</small><h3>Institutional pilot learning</h3><p>Test real operational fit with participating educators and refine quality, usability, and data handling.</p></div></div><div style="font-size:10px;color:#98a4b4;margin-top:20px">Planned roadmap · No completion dates implied</div></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="container"><div class="quote reveal"><div class="eyebrow">Leadership perspective</div><h2>“The most valuable role for AI in education is not to replace the teacher, but to give every educator and learner more room to grow.”</h2><div class="quote-bottom"><div><strong>Hoang Hieu</strong><span>CEO · Bright Education JSC.</span></div><div class="monogram">BE / AI</div></div><p style="font-size:10px;color:#9eabc6;margin-top:22px;position:relative;z-index:1">Editorial leadership statement for website concept; confirm wording with the CEO before publication.</p></div></section>
<section class="contact" id="contact"><div class="container split"><div class="reveal"><div class="eyebrow">Let's build what's next</div><h2 class="section-title">Better learning<br>starts with a conversation.</h2><p class="section-copy">We welcome conversations with language schools, education providers, curriculum specialists, and technical collaborators interested in responsible AI applications for learning.</p><div class="contact-info"><div><span>Email</span><a href="mailto:info@brighteducation.net">info@brighteducation.net</a></div><div><span>Location</span><p>1-10-3 Honmachi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, Japan</p></div><div><span>Company</span><p>Bright Education JSC. · CEO: Hoang Hieu</p></div></div></div><div class="contact-panel reveal"><div class="eyebrow">Partnership inquiries</div><h3 style="margin-top:20px">Tell us what you're working on.</h3><p>Have a school workflow, language teaching challenge, or AI education idea you'd like to explore? Start an email conversation with our team.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:info@brighteducation.net?subject=Bright%20Education%20-%20Partnership%20Inquiry&body=Hello%20Bright%20Education%20team%2C%0A%0AI%20would%20like%20to%20discuss%3A%0A%0A">Email our team <span class="small-arrow">↗</span></a><small>No account, signup, or data submission is required on this website.</small></div></div></section>
</main><footer class="footer"><div class="container"><div class="footer-main"><div><a href="#home" class="logo"><img class="brandmark brand-logo" src="/assets/images/favicon.png" alt="Bright Education logo">bright<span style="color:#6978a7;margin-left:-10px">education</span></a><p class="footer-desc">Thoughtful AI technology for education, language development, and a more connected learning experience.</p></div><div class="foot-links"><a href="#solutions">Solutions</a><a href="#approach">Approach</a><a href="#use-cases">Use cases</a><a href="#about">About</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></div></div><div class="footer-bottom"><span>© <span id="year">2026</span> Bright Education JSC. All rights reserved.</span><span>Product illustrations use fictional data. Features are concepts under development.</span></div></div></footer>
<script>document.getElementById('year').textContent=new Date().getFullYear();const menuBtn=document.getElementById('menuBtn'),navLinks=document.getElementById('navLinks');menuBtn.addEventListener('click',()=>{const isOpen=navLinks.classList.toggle('open');menuBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(isOpen));menuBtn.textContent=isOpen?'×':'☰'});navLinks.querySelectorAll('a').forEach(link=>link.addEventListener('click',()=>{navLinks.classList.remove('open');menuBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');menuBtn.textContent='☰'}));if('IntersectionObserver'in window){const observer=new IntersectionObserver(entries=>entries.forEach(e=>{if(e.isIntersecting){e.target.classList.add('visible');observer.unobserve(e.target)}}),{threshold:.08});document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el=>observer.observe(el))}else document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el=>el.classList.add('visible'));</script>
